<h2 id="access-and-safety">RV access and safety</h2>
<p>You are responsible for arranging permission to access the RV and service location, including any dealer, owner, storage-facility, or campground approval. Please provide accurate RV information, disclose known hazards, and arrange any utilities or preparations we identify in advance. We may decline or stop work that cannot be performed safely or without proper authorization.</p>

<h2 id="training-and-consulting">Training, walkthroughs, and consulting</h2>
<p>Training and consulting help you understand your RV and make informed decisions. They do not replace the manufacturer's instructions, required maintenance, qualified repairs, or legal, financial, or insurance advice. Pre-purchase consulting provides information and comparisons; the final purchase decision remains yours. Recommendations are based on the information available at the time.</p>
<p>Package hours, availability periods, follow-up consulting, video recordings, and delivery arrangements are those stated in the offering and confirmed when you book. Recording is included only when purchased or expressly agreed. You may use delivered training materials and videos for your personal RV ownership and operation; please obtain permission before publishing or commercially redistributing them.</p>

<h2 id="maintenance-and-concierge">Maintenance and concierge services</h2>
<p>Maintenance and repairs are limited to the work agreed upon. A diagnosis does not authorize additional repairs automatically. Concierge visits cover the scheduled checks described in your agreement; they do not provide continuous monitoring, security, emergency response, or a guarantee against damage, theft, pests, or equipment failure.</p>

<h2 id="inspection-terms">RV inspections</h2>
<p>An inspection reports the condition of accessible items evaluated within the agreed scope at the time of inspection. Conditions can change, and concealed, intermittent, or inaccessible defects may not be detected. An inspection is not a warranty, insurance policy, appraisal, or guarantee of future performance, and it cannot identify every possible defect.</p>
<p>Your inspection agreement defines the inspection scope, exclusions, preparation requirements, report delivery, and permitted use of the report. An inspection does not replace specialized evaluations or manufacturer recall checks outside its agreed scope. Purchase, repair, and travel decisions remain yours.</p>
